# PROJECT: CAMPUSLOOP
## COMPLETE BACKEND DEVELOPMENT, DATABASE INTEGRATION AND PRODUCTION IMPLEMENTATION

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, backend architect, PostgreSQL database engineer, SaaS security specialist and marketplace platform developer.

Your task is to transform the existing CampusLoop application from a frontend prototype into a fully functional, secure and production-ready multi-university marketplace.

IMPORTANT: THIS IS AN EXISTING PROJECT.

The frontend has already been designed and developed using Lovable.

Do not unnecessarily redesign, rebuild or replace the existing frontend.

First inspect the complete existing codebase, understand its architecture, pages, components, navigation, UI/UX, design system and existing functionality.

Preserve the existing:
- Branding.
- Colour system.
- Typography.
- Animations.
- Layouts.
- Responsive behaviour.
- Navigation.
- User experience.
- Existing application structure.

Your primary responsibility is to implement the complete backend, database, authentication, file storage, marketplace logic, analytics, security and frontend-backend integration.

Do not simply create a new application.

==================================================
1. PRODUCT DEFINITION
==================================================

CampusLoop is a Ghanaian university marketplace and student services discovery platform.

It connects:

1. Students looking to purchase products.
2. Students selling products.
3. Students offering services.
4. Businesses serving university communities.

The platform supports multiple universities in Ghana.

Users should be able to discover products and services based on their selected university or browse listings across all supported universities.

CampusLoop is NOT an e-commerce payment platform.

CRITICAL BUSINESS MODEL REQUIREMENTS:

- Do not implement payments.
- Do not implement checkout.
- Do not implement shopping carts.
- Do not implement order processing.
- Do not implement transaction commissions.
- Do not collect money on behalf of sellers.
- Do not charge commissions on transactions.
- Do not create payment gateways.

CampusLoop only connects buyers with sellers and service providers.

Buyers contact sellers directly through their preferred contact methods.

The platform should remain simple, lightweight, visually attractive and easy to operate.

