21. DATABASE SECURITY
==================================================

Security is a critical requirement.

Implement PostgreSQL Row Level Security on all appropriate tables.

Policies must ensure:

PUBLIC USERS:
- Can view active and approved listings.
- Can view public seller profiles.
- Can view active universities and categories.
- Cannot access private seller account information.
- Cannot create or modify listings.

AUTHENTICATED SELLERS:
- Can create listings.
- Can edit their own listings.
- Can archive their own listings.
- Can manage their own profile.
- Can view their own listing analytics.
- Cannot modify other sellers' listings.

ADMINISTRATORS:
- Can perform authorized moderation.
- Can manage universities.
- Can manage categories.
- Can manage users.
- Can access administrative analytics.

Important:

Never rely on frontend route protection alone.

Never trust seller_id or user_id supplied by the frontend without validating the authenticated user.

Do not allow users to assign themselves administrator permissions.

Use secure database functions and Edge Functions where appropriate.

Do not expose the service-role key.

Implement rate limiting or abuse controls for sensitive public operations.

Protect against:

- Unauthorized listing modifications.
- Spam listings.
- Excessive contact-click submissions.
- Malicious file uploads.
- Unauthorized administrative actions.
- Enumeration of private user data.

